    "title": "",
    "legend": "Distribution of mutations in the <em>CEBPA</em> gene. In cases with biallelic mutations in <em>CEBPA</em>, almost all somatic N-terminal mutations are located in the N-terminal direction from the p30 start codon&nbsp;{20439648}, located at amino acid (aa)&nbsp;120. In cases with a single mutation, the mutation should be located in the bZIP region in order to confer the diagnosis of AML with <em>CEBPA</em> mutation {33951732; 34320176; 34448807}. DBD,&nbsp;DNA-binding domain; LZD&nbsp;leucine zipper domain; TAD,&nbsp;transactivation domain.",
